mindyourhead-by-macslow (1.0-0ddebs3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Changes prepared with Claude Opus 5.5
  * Fix startup on systems without libsdl2-dev and libgl-dev: the intro
    dlopen()s libSDL2-2.0.so and libGL.so, debian/*.links now provides
    these names in the executable directory and the launcher sets
    LD_LIBRARY_PATH
  * debian/control : added libgl1 dependency, fixed common-install-
    function-ddebs relation, real description
  * debian/resources : added the missing icon (from the pouet.net
    screenshot), Keywords in the .desktop file
  * debian/scripts : enable V-Sync with __GL_SYNC_TO_VBLANK=1 by default
  * debian/mindyourhead-by-macslow.6.md : real content, regenerated man
    page
  * debian/README.source, debian/copyright : details about the prebuilt
    executable and upstream archive
  * debian/upstream/metadata.ex : removed template leftover
  * debian/rules : compute ${shlibs:Depends} on debian/shlibs-stub.c, as
    dpkg-shlibdeps cannot read the packed executable (fixes lintian
    missing-dependency-on-libc)
  * debian/mindyourhead-by-macslow.lintian-overrides : hardening-no-pie
    on the prebuilt executable, groff-message from the pandoc preamble

